Soulvizier 0.98i ported to Titan Quest Anniversary Edition - the classic souls overhaul, playable again, plus new content.

[b]Status:[/b] Under active development and updated often, and playable start to finish through Epic difficulty. It is honestly still a work in progress, so save often and please leave feedback in the comments - it directly shapes what I fix next. Known issues are listed below.

[h1]Features[/h1]
[list]
[*] 800+ monster souls to collect and equip, including 60 boss souls, most newly completed (summon-the-boss and boss-skill souls)
[*] Souls have LEVEL requirements only, exactly like classic Soulvizier. No strength, dexterity, or intelligence gates on souls.
[*] The original Soulvizier secret areas restored (see below)
[*] New superboss: a blood-soaked incarnation of Toxeus the Murderer guarding the secret area, with the Crimson Verdict legendary set
[*] All the classic masteries with Occult overhauled and improved, plus your DLC masteries (Neidan, Runemaster); legacy skills restored
[*] Classic reward potions are in and dropping: skill point, attribute point, and experience potions appear as rare drops in the same loot slot relics come from. Experience potions are also sold by Greece market mages, and all three types can be crafted at the forge.
[*] Epic and legendary enchanting, improved pet summons
[*] The campaign ends at the Immortal Throne (Hades), like the original Soulvizier
[/list]

[h1]How is this different from SVAERA?[/h1]
Both mods bring Soulvizier to Anniversary Edition. Soulvizier Classic preserves the classic 0.98i experience:
[list]
[*] Souls: level requirement only. In SVAERA nearly every soul also requires strength, dexterity, or intelligence; here your build is never stat-gated out of its souls.
[*] The original Soulvizier areas are restored and reachable in the campaign world (see the list below).
[*] The Occult mastery is overhauled and improved here (hand-tuned skills and balance).
[*] Classic pacing and endpoint: the run ends at Hades, as Soulvizier always did.
[/list]

[h1]Restored Soulvizier areas[/h1]
[list]
[*] The Blood Cave: the signature Soulvizier dungeon, about 24 levels deep, in the Hidden Valley on the Silk Road. Walk into the natural cave and take the west tunnel. Questlines (the Grieving Widow and more), an occultist camp with a respawn fountain and the Super-Caravan, hidden chambers, and the secret waterfall chamber where the blood superboss waits.
[*] Uber Dungeon: portal in the Minotaur Lord's boss room in the Knossos labyrinth.
[*] Boss Arena: reached through the Uber Dungeon's quest progression.
[*] Garden of Merchants: portal at the Hidden Valley camp, next to the respawn fountain.
[*] The Secret Place: an 11-level dark forest, via a portal tucked into the east edge of the Rhodes Secret Vista.
[*] Sparta Crypt depths: portal in the deepest chamber of the catacombs under the Athens battlefield (a brand new entrance; the original never had one).
[/list]
Getting back out: the Garden of Merchants and the Secret Place use the rift/teleport SHRINE inside the area (the classic Soulvizier way back), and the Uber Dungeon has a return door in its deepest crypt.

[h1]Known issues / work in progress[/h1]
I am actively fixing these, and the list is updated as fixes ship. Save often.
[list]
[*] Several mastery skill pages show a black background instead of the proper artwork. It is cosmetic and does not affect your skills. Fix in progress.
[*] Some skills are misplaced or missing their icons in the mastery trees. A full audit of every mastery is underway.
[*] Damage numbers are not displaying over enemies right now. Under investigation.
[*] Language switching does not work yet, so the mod is English only for now. Under investigation.
[*] FIXED: Toxeus the Enslaver, the roaming shadow mini-boss, no longer turns up everywhere - he now haunts undead packs only, so he is a rare surprise. The dependable way to fight him is his placed warband set-piece.
[*] A rare crash can happen deep in the Blood Cave. Save often while you are down there; a fix is in progress.
[*] IMPORTANT: items already in your bags keep the stats they had when they dropped. If a soul you picked up before an update has a granted skill that does not activate, that specific item stays broken; newly dropped copies work. This is how the game engine stores items, not something we can patch retroactively.
[*] Exploding sprites near the occultist pyre may not respawn, and Blood Cave smoke density is still being tuned toward classic levels.
[/list]

[h1]Found a bug?[/h1]
Please leave a comment below describing what you ran into: where you were, what you expected, and what happened. I read everything and will address issues as I can. Fixes and update notes get posted here.

[h1]Requirements and how to play[/h1]
[list]
[*] Requires Titan Quest Anniversary Edition.
[*] REQUIRES the Eternal Embers expansion. If the mod fails to launch, or the map list looks wrong, or you get sent back to the menu, you are almost certainly missing Eternal Embers. This is the number one cause of the mod not working.
[*] MULTIPLAYER requires ALL expansions (Ragnarok, Atlantis, Eternal Embers) for EVERY player. This total conversion merges all-expansion content into one world, and the game bounces joiners missing any of them with a get-DLC prompt. That prompt may open an empty Steam cart (a Steam bug); buy from the expansion store pages directly. Single-player works without Ragnarok/Atlantis, but you cannot enter their regions, so all expansions are strongly recommended.
[*] Play via Custom Quest > SoulvizierClassic with a dedicated Custom Quest character. Never load a normal-campaign character into the mod.
[*] Strongly recommended: the community 4GB LAA patch for TQ.exe (this is a large mod). Steam's verify-integrity feature reverts it, so re-apply it after verifying files.
[*] Multiplayer: up to 6 players; everyone must be on the same mod version (let Steam finish updating the mod before hosting).
[/list]

[h1]Updates[/h1]
2026-07-10 (sixth update): New content. Throwing weapons return to the whole campaign (they drop from Act 1-4 monsters again), plus three craftable legendary throwing weapons - Sanguine Orbit, The Last Word, and Charon's Toll. Toxeus the Murderer returns as the Enslaver of Souls, a towering ShadowStalker who roams the world as a rare mini-boss with a warband of shadow marauders; his soul fights at your side. Sepulchral wyrm hordes pour out of the Orient tombs, their champions dropping the new Sepulchral Scale armor charm. Long Nu the Flame Mother is fixed (proper summon-pet button, full strength). Mastery wave 2 tunes Warfare, Nature, Spirit, Dream, Runemaster and Neidan. Coming next: an Obsidian Halls boss roulette, the warlord Vashkarr near Chang'an, and a Portal Master in Helos.

2026-07-10 (fifth update): Kill Typhon and the Rhodes portal opens instantly. Four new summon souls (Eater of Days, Pygmalion, War-King Sarpedon, Long Nu). Mastery wave 1 got many skills casting and hurting again (Meteor, Thunderball, Bonespire, Shield Smash, Batter, Volcanic Orb, Colossus, Rally). Shadow Stalker and the Core Dweller golem are much stronger, and the Boss Arena boss, widow moral-choice branch, and Chimera epic chest are fixed.

2026-07-08 to 09 (earlier updates): the campaign was opened past Typhon toward Hades (the Rhodes portal now unlocks); the four classic Soulvizier questlines (Grieving Widow, sealed temple door, Esti chest, Boss Arena) load and track; soul-granted attack skills fire on fresh drops and boss-soul pets render; boss-summon souls were added (Xeiwang, Huo-ren, the blood superboss, Narok, Vort); and the starter co-op chest, gold portals, Sparta Crypt two-way door, Secret Place return shrine, superboss red shroud, 200+ dead granted skills, Occult naming, and the Workshop packaging were all fixed.
